# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repository AND in every working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: Windows clones run with core.autocrlf=true, so a
# checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF. Prettier has no `endOfLine` set in
# .prettierrc and therefore defaults to "lf". The result was that
# `npx prettier --check src scripts tests` flagged 101 files on Windows and
# zero on the Linux CI runner -- a red check that said nothing about the code.
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree too, so both platforms see identical bytes and
# the local check matches CI.
#
# The repo tracks only text (yaml, ts, md, json) -- no binaries, and no
# CRLF-dependent scripts such as .bat or .cmd -- so one blanket rule is enough.
# The explicit `binary` lines below are a guard for files added later, since
# `text=auto` would otherwise have to guess.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
